# Context: 200k tokens
# Strengths: Follows instructions precisely, good at complex refactors
# Weaknesses: Slower, more expensive
# Safety: Generally stays on rails
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs
#
# Claude defaults to prompting for tool permissions per session. Keep the safer
# permission model (no bypass), but allow common dev commands to avoid repeated
# confirmations for basics like git/gh/rg/ls/cat plus curl/wget for web fetches.
#
# Note: use repeated --allowed-tools=... so the option parser does not consume
# the user prompt argument (Claude treats --allowed-tools as a variadic list).
claude --permission-mode acceptEdits --allowed-tools='Bash(git:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(gh:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(rg:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(ls:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(cat:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(sed:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(awk:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(head:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(tail:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(curl:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(wget:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(find:*)' --allowed-tools='Bash(stat:*)' --allowed-tools=Read --allowed-tools=Edit
